    <bpmn:process id="W_W4726" name="W4726. Third-Party Data Classification &amp; Data-Access/Processing Risk Scoping" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New third party; data-access change; privacy review (VS-91)
Frequency: Per third party + on change
Volume: ~ all third parties with data access (SaaS, BPO, payment, marketplace, fraud/CDP providers)
Owner: TPRM Program Manager (joint with Privacy VS-91)
Participants: Privacy (VS-91), Cyber (VS-27.3), Data Governance (VS-28), Legal (VS-100.3), business owners
Source: workflow W4726 — Third-Party Data Classification &amp; Data-Access/Processing Risk Scoping</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4726_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4726_Lane1" name="TPRM Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4726_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4726_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4726_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4726_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4726_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4726_Start3" name="New third party; data-access change; privacy review (VS-91)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4726_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4726_Task4" name="For each third party, scope data-access: what BuildRight/customer/employee data…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For each third party, scope data-access: what BuildRight/customer/employee data the third party (and fourth parties W4724) can access/process (PII VS-91, payment data PCI, credentials, IP); classify the data sensitivity
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Privacy / Cyber
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / DPO
Duration: Per third party</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4726_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4726_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4726_Task5" name="Determine the data-protection posture required (DPA, transfer mechanism for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Determine the data-protection posture required (DPA, transfer mechanism for cross-border, encryption, access controls, retention/disposal) per VS-91; scope privacy DD (W4731) and cyber DD (W4730) accordingly
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Privacy / Cyber / Legal
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / DPO / CIO
Duration: Per third party</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4726_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4726_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4726_Task6" name="Monitor data-access changes (scope creep, new data type, sub-processor W4724)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monitor data-access changes (scope creep, new data type, sub-processor W4724); manage unauthorized data-access/use; ensure data-return/deletion on exit (W4740)
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Privacy / Cyber
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / DPO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4726_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4726_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4726_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4726_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-167 (ensure third-party risk tiering &amp; oversight.) | - CTL-713: data-access scoped and classified; DPA/transfer mechanism per VS-91; changes monitored; exit data-return (W4740)
Owner: TPRM Program Manager (joint with Privacy VS-91)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
