    <bpmn:process id="W_W4728" name="W4728. TPRM Governance, Ownership Matrix &amp; Board Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Governance review; board cycle (VS-36); significant event
Frequency: Quarterly + on event
Volume: 1 TPRM governance &amp; reporting cadence
Owner: TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Participants: Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (VS-21.2), Compliance (VS-22), business/function owners, Board Risk Committee (VS-36)
Source: workflow W4728 — TPRM Governance, Ownership Matrix &amp; Board Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4728_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4728_Lane1" name="TPRM Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4728_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4728_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4728_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4728_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4728_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4728_Start3" name="Governance review; board cycle (VS-36); significant event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4728_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4728_Task4" name="Maintain the TPRM governance &amp; ownership matrix: each third party has a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain the TPRM governance &amp; ownership matrix: each third party has a business owner (the function that uses it) and a risk-domain owner (privacy/cyber/ABC/etc.); the TPRM Program owns the backbone; define escalation paths
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4728_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4728_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4728_Task5" name="Report TPRM to the board risk committee (VS-36) quarterly: third-party…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Report TPRM to the board risk committee (VS-36) quarterly: third-party inventory summary, Critical/High exposure, concentration (W4725), significant findings (PA-161.2), resilience posture (PA-161.3); integrate into ERM reporting (VS-21.2)
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / Board
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4728_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4728_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4728_Task6" name="Manage significant TPRM events (Critical third-party failure, breach…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage significant TPRM events (Critical third-party failure, breach, concentration shock) with executive/board notification per the ERM escalation (VS-21.2/W4694); assure via Internal Audit (VS-21)
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / Board
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4728_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4728_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4728_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4728_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-167 (ensure third-party risk tiering &amp; oversight.) | - CTL-713: every third party has a business + risk-domain owner; board reported quarterly; significant events escalated (VS-21.2)
Owner: TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
